div.p:
2. Concrete issues, however, are more easily resolved but only if they have been
                    well prepared and the Soviets do not have to contend with surprises that have
                    not been aired by the collective leadership;

4. Meeting the “people” is of little interest to the Soviets. Their preoccupation
                    is with those who have the power of decision (this, incidentally, is why
                    Congressional delegations do so poorly in the USSR);
